  source_columns:
    count: 3-6 distinct columns in row 0
    extent: contiguous vertical stripe from row 0 down to obs_row-2 or obs_row-1 (gap 0-1 to obstacle)
    spacing: gaps of 2-4 between adjacent source cols [observed]
  obstacle:
    single_row: one row, position at roughly 40-50% of grid height (row 4-5)
    segments: 1-2 contiguous horizontal runs, each length 2-4
    no_edge_touch: segments never occupy col 0 or col W-1
    gap_between_segments: >=1 col when multiple segments
  detours:
    at_least_one: >=1 source col must overlap an obstacle segment
    no_destination_collision: each detoured col routes to nearest free side col; no two sources share a destination
    no_path_overlap: horizontal detour path on row obs_row-1 must not cross another source col
    tie_break: equidistant cols detour to right side
    detour_distance: 1-2 cols [observed]
  below_obstacle: all cells are bg in input (no content below obstacle row except obstacle itself)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first (build settled output, then strip trajectory to get input)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid dims (H 9-10, W 10-15), source color, obstacle color.
    2. Pick obs_row in [3, H//2] and source extent rows 0..obs_row-2 or 0..obs_row-1.
    3. Place 1-2 obstacle segments on obs_row, each length 2-4, not touching grid edges, with >=1 col gap between segments.
    4. Choose 3-6 destination columns below the obstacle (these are the final vertical lines in output). Ensure no destination falls inside an obstacle segment and no duplicates.
    5. For each destination col, determine if it is adjacent to an obstacle segment side. If so, pick a source col inside that segment (nearest to that side) such that it detours to the destination. If not, the source col equals the destination col. Verify no source col collisions, no detour path crosses another source col.
    6. Build output by painting full vertical lines at destination cols (rows 0..H-1 except obstacle cells), plus horizontal detour runs on obs_row-1, plus source-col verticals from row 0 to obs_row-1.
    7. Derive input by keeping only source-col verticals from row 0 to source extent bottom and the obstacle segments; erase all trajectory paint.
